spans.s:
ápa, prep. away, forth, off; opp. of úpa,
see √√i, kṛ. [cf. ἀπό, Lat. ab, ‘from’;
Eng. off, of.]

ápara [525], pron. a. hinder, opp. of pūrva;
following a former one (pūrva), 86^13;
later; westerly, opp. to pūrva--cf. prāñc;
a following one, i. e. an other; aparaṃ ca,
and another thing, and further, see ca 3;
--aparī́ [cf. 355b], f. pl. the future
(days), the future. [lit. ‘remoter,’ fr. ápa,
474.]

ápa-vrata, a. disobedient; stubborn.
[‘away from command,’ 1310a: cf. ánuvrata.
]
